{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | sed -n '242,287p;648,670p;1311,1365p;1486,1501p'\nnl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '260,284p;579,691p;1520,1566p;1858,1881p'\nnl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '685,762p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md | sed -n '242,287p;648,670p;1311,1365p;1486,1501p'\nnl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | sed -n '260,284p;579,691p;1520,1566p;1858,1881p'\nnl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ucf-phase2/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc | sed -n '685,762p'\"","aggregated_output":"   242\tbyte encoding lands, `:yin.code/hash` values change with every other minted\n   243\taddress. This is the correct dependency; UCF must not mint a second\n   244\taddressing scheme.\n   245\t\n   246\t### 7.3.3 The contract stamp\n   247\t\n   248\tAn address fixes *which* instructions; it does not fix what `:call` *means*.\n   249\tInterpretation is supplied by the loader and the step loop (§1.1,\n   250\t*Interpretation Creates Semantics*), and the first draft pinned only the\n   251\topcode table — leaving resolution precedence, effect outcomes, call\n   252\trestoration, and scheduling outside the stamp. UCF therefore versions the\n   253\t**complete execution contract**: the stamp names one published revision of\n   254\t\n   255\t- the tuple grammar of §7.3.2 — the mnemonic set, each mnemonic's tuple\n   256\t  arity and operand kinds, and the saturation/defaults table — plus the\n   257\t  §2.6 well-formedness rules and the resolved-interpretation\n   258\t  (last-value-wins) rule;\n   259\t- the §2.4 opcode table and the §4.2 transitions;\n   260\t- the resolution precedence of `resolve-var` (env → store → primitives →\n   261\t  modules);\n   262\t- the effect→outcome mapping of §3.3 and `engine/handle-effect`;\n   263\t- call restoration and the scheduler semantics of §3.5 — wait-entry shapes,\n   264\t  `check-wait-set`'s round order, `semantic-restore`.\n   265\t\n   266\t```clojure\n   267\t:yin.k/contract {:yin.code/contract \"v2\"    ; the revision above, by name\n   268\t                 :yin.k/version    0}       ; this envelope's own version\n   269\t```\n   270\t\n   271\tA resumer whose loader implements a different revision does not guess: it\n   272\treturns `:yin.k/profile-mismatch` (§7.9) *before* lowering. Adding an opcode,\n   273\tchanging a transition, or changing the resolution order is a new revision; a\n   274\tresumer on the old one cannot run code that observes the difference, and the\n   275\tstamp is how it finds out before lowering rather than at an unknown integer\n   276\tin `case`. Two revisions may be declared compatible only by a published\n   277\tstatement in `yin.vm.semantic.md` §2.4, never by an engine's own judgment.\n   278\tBecause interpretation is part of identity, an engine's code index is keyed\n   279\t**per stamp revision**: lookup is `(get-in index [stamp address])`, and the\n   280\tsame address under different stamps is a different image the same way the\n   281\tsame datoms under different loaders are a different program.\n   282\t\n   283\t### 7.3.4 References to code inside a continuation\n   284\t\n   285\tEvery place the local record says `:segment <id>` — the control, each\n   286\t`:return` frame, each effect frame, each closure's `:segment` — the UCF frame\n   287\tsays `:yin.k/segment <address>`. Entry pcs and frame pcs are unchanged: a pc\n   648\t  (`:yin.k/non-portable`, kind `:ambiguous-primitive`) unless the\n   649\t  composition declares a canonical-name table resolving it to exactly one.\n   650\t- **A host function under no name is refused** (kind `:unnamed-function`) —\n   651\t  a bridge handler's return value, a module-constructed function: it has no\n   652\t  declared semantics to travel under.\n   653\t- **`:host`-class functions are refused** (kind `:host-state-primitive`). A\n   654\t  function whose behavior depends on undeclared host state is not a value\n   655\t  any other host can honor; profiles that declare host state may not be\n   656\t  lifted, and a profile claiming `:host-state :none` is a publication's\n   657\t  warranty, versioned with the contract stamp's primitive-profile registry.\n   658\t- **On lowering, the resumer's binding is checked by profile, not by\n   659\t  presence.** For each required name, the resumer must hold a primitive\n   660\t  whose profile address is equal; a same-named function of different profile\n   661\t  is `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the symbol and the expected profile — it is\n   662\t  a routing decision for whoever chose this resumer, not a silent\n   663\t  substitution.\n   664\t- The standard map `yin.vm/primitives` must be published with profiles\n   665\t  (note `yin/def` is `:effectful` with effect `:vm/store-put`, and `require`\n   666\t  is `:effectful` with `:module/require`); that publication is an acceptance\n   667\t  blocker (§7.11).\n   668\t\n   669\t### 7.5.3 Sharing, cells, and cycles\n   670\t\n  1311\t## §7.11 Acceptance blockers for the implementation phase\n  1312\t\n  1313\tThe warning at the top of this file is retained until each of these is\n  1314\tclosed with a test in the parity or conformance suite. The first four are\n  1315\tthe review's named architectural obligations; they are blockers to\n  1316\t*accepting the design*, not merely work items.\n  1317\t\n  1318\t- **Authority grounding and wiring.** The arbitration `dao.space`, its\n  1319\t  transactor as grantor, the occurrence ledger with epochs, and the\n  1320\t  attribution resolver `dao.lease.md` requires, are composition duties; the\n  1321\t  first composition to ship UCF is `yin.repl.core`'s handoff demo, and\n  1322\t  its wiring becomes the worked example. A composition without a\n  1323\t  transactable space offers `:yin.k/fork` only.\n  1324\t- **Execution identity.** Occurrence minting, the `:yin.k/origin` chain,\n  1325\t  retry idempotence (one occurrence per park), and successor completion as\n  1326\t  a grantor ledger transition need conformance tests, including the crash\n  1327\t  windows of §7.7.5.\n  1328\t- **Pending-state completeness.** Every pending variant of §7.4.3 must\n  1329\t  round-trip and resume *elsewhere*: retained writes, sent and retained FFI\n  1330\t  calls with both endpoints and the kept response cursor, and cursor cells\n  1331\t  through the aliasing scenarios of `check-wait-set`. This depends on a\n  1332\t  generated stream-over-network facade and a **portable cursor profile**\n  1333\t  that preserves the source stream's kept cursor and `gap` outcomes. The\n  1334\t  M4 string-backed stream test below is the required cross-host proof.\n  1335\t- **Enforceable fencing.** Epoch-checked, atomic-with-commitment admission\n  1336\t  and durable op-id plus intent dedup at enrolled consumers are design\n  1337\t  items for `dao.space.transactor.md`. A consumer without a shared atomic\n  1338\t  boundary declares at-least-once or fail-stop behavior; it cannot claim\n  1339\t  exactly-once custody from the lease alone.\n  1340\t- **Canonical byte encoding.** `:yin.code/hash` and `:yin.k/id` are exactly\n  1341\t  as portable as `dao.jing/segment-key`. Canonical CBOR landed in\n  1342\t  3ddaa21b (recorded in `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` section 5); the\n  1343\t  cross-host address checks below still must pass.\n  1344\t- **Contract revision publication.** `:yin.code/contract \"v2\"` has a\n  1345\t  published revision history naming the complete execution contract\n  1346\t  (§7.3.3): the tuple grammar — mnemonic set, per-mnemonic arity and operand\n  1347\t  kinds, saturation/defaults table — the opcode table and transitions, the\n  1348\t  resolution and last-value-wins rules, the effect outcome map, and the\n  1349\t  scheduler semantics. The index is in `yin.vm.semantic.md` 2.4 and the\n  1350\t  history landed in dbae125b (`yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md`); runtime profile\n  1351\t  checks below remain open.\n  1352\t- **Primitive profile publication.** The standard `yin.vm/primitives`\n  1353\t  map published with profiles (§7.5.2), including the `:effectful`\n  1354\t  declarations for `yin/def` and `require`; reverse-lookup uniqueness\n  1355\t  asserted at `create-vm`.\n  1356\t- **Discovery completeness.** The fixed point of §7.6.1 implemented and\n  1357\t  tested against the `:store-get`/`:store-put`, dynamic-callee, and\n  1358\t  cross-activation-`E` cases; module manifests publishing store footprints\n  1359\t  so `:yin.k/discovery :incomplete` disappears.\n  1360\t- **Isolated-store lowering.** Conformance tests that the resumed task's\n  1361\t  store contains exactly the slice and the resumer's pair, and that a\n  1362\t  receiver-side binding of a name in the slice's name set cannot change\n  1363\t  resolution.\n  1364\t- **Safepoint conformance harness.** A test that runs every corpus segment\n  1365\t  on the reference machine to each safepoint of the complete §7.4.1 table —\n  1486\t- Action and expected outcome: Lift, transfer, and lower on each host;\n  1487\t  literals remain literals, repeated refs share one value, independent\n  1488\t  cursor cells advance independently, and shared cells advance in wait\n  1489\t  order. The lift refuses unsupported leaves as `:yin.k/non-portable`\n  1490\t  with path and kind and publishes no partial value; decode refuses\n  1491\t  malformed markers and refs as `:yin.k/undecodable` with path before\n  1492\t  restoring state. Forged resource refs refuse before lift, while valid\n  1493\t  refs re-seal on lower into the receiver's private resource table. A\n  1494\t  same-named primitive with a different profile is `:yin.k/unsatisfied`,\n  1495\t  never substituted by name alone.\n  1496\t- Landing and order: M4 supplies the recursive codec, published standard\n  1497\t  primitive profiles (including effectful `yin/def` and `require`), and\n  1498\t  linker section 11 item 12's `:yin.k/binding`, `:yin.k/store-of`,\n  1499\t  private-resource, and sealed-reference variants before lift uses them.\n  1500\t  M4 also proves the string-backed stream facade and kept-cursor case in\n  1501\t  the safepoint row before cross-host values are accepted. Phase 1\n   260\t :obligations-fn      (fn [value] records)           ; step 5a, below\n   261\t :definitions-fn      (fn [value] records)           ; step 5a, below\n   262\t :applications-fn     (fn [value] records)           ; step 5a, below\n   263\t :parts-fn            (fn [value] [address ...])}   ; step 2 worklist\n   264\t```\n   265\t\n   266\t- `:identity-fn` mints an identity from a payload. It is used by\n   267\t  `publish!` and never by verification.\n   268\t- `:identity-matches-fn` is the step-3 check, directed by the identity.\n   269\t  For H and R it is `(= identity (image-hash value))`, a contract-pinned\n   270\t  hash with one algorithm. For the storage-derived formats it is\n   271\t  `(jing/segment-matches? identity value)`, so a value minted under\n   272\t  `:sha256` while the default is `:blake3` verifies under the algorithm\n   273\t  the identity names and never fails spuriously.\n   274\t- `:row-defect-fn` validates one fetched part on its own, before any\n   275\t  address it references is enqueued: tag, arity, slot kinds, saturation.\n   276\t  For single-payload formats it is the whole validator, run early.\n   277\t- `:parts-fn` returns the storage addresses a fetched payload references\n   278\t  and without which it is incomplete. For the three single-payload\n   279\t  formats it returns nothing. For `:yin.ast/code` it returns the child\n   280\t  row ids of a row body.\n   281\t- `:obligations-fn`, `:definitions-fn`, and `:applications-fn` are\n   282\t  **position-bearing scanners** with one shared result shape:\n   283\t\n   284\t  ```clojure\n   579\t\n   580\t`:unsupported-format` is the linker's instance of the host-boundary rule\n   581\tthat a host with no implementation for an effect emits a qualified\n   582\tunsupported result, \"a correct outcome, not a gap to be filled\"\n   583\t(`datom.world.md`). It lets a receiver decline an R request and, where\n   584\tthe composition permits, fall back to H by the manifest's derivations.\n   585\t\n   586\tA stepped link additionally reports `:pending` (section 6.3), which is\n   587\tnot a refusal: it is the \"not yet\" of a non-blocking read.\n   588\t\n   589\t## 5. Format records for the four backends\n   590\t\n   591\tThree records bind existing code; the AST record's free-name scanner is\n   592\tthe section 4.5 query of `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`, implemented as\n   593\t`yin.vm/free-names`.\n   594\t\n   595\t### 5.1 `:yin.ast/code` (the AST walker)\n   596\t\n   597\t```clojure\n   598\t{:format              :yin.ast/code\n   599\t :contract            \"v2\"\n   600\t :identity-fn         (fn [body] (jing/segment-key body))\n   601\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [root-id body] (jing/segment-matches? root-id\n   602\t                                                                  body))\n   603\t :row-defect-fn       (fn [body] (row-local-defect body))\n   604\t :validate-fn         (fn [tree] (yin.vm/validate-rows tree))\n   605\t :obligations-fn      (fn [tree] (free-name-occurrences tree))\n   606\t :definitions-fn      (fn [tree] (definition-occurrences tree))\n   607\t :applications-fn     (fn [tree] (application-sites tree))\n   608\t :parts-fn            (fn [body] (body-child-ids body))}\n   609\t```\n   610\t\n   611\tPayload: one row body `[tag & slots]` per address, exactly as\n   612\t`yin.vm.content/materialize-tree!` stores it (D3: individual rows, no pack\n   613\tformat; the body is what is hashed, and the id is derived from it). The\n   614\tidentity is the root row's id. Steps 2 and 3 therefore hash the fetched\n   615\tbody as received; the address is prepended only when the linker assembles\n   616\t`{id [id tag & slots]}` for step 4, the shape `validate-rows` takes.\n   617\t`row-local-defect` runs the `:tag`, `:arity`, `:slot-kind`, and\n   618\t`:saturation` rules of section 7.4 over one body, so a malformed row\n   619\tnever has its slots followed. Step 2's worklist follows `node` and\n   620\t`nodes` slots by the grammar's positions, the walk\n   621\t`yin.vm.content/load-rows` performs today; that function's throwing\n   622\tsurface is retired in favor of the linker's refusals (section 9).\n   623\tAll three scanners return the position-bearing records of section\n   624\t4.1: `free-name-occurrences` is `yin.vm/free-names` wrapped to carry\n   625\teach occurrence's path and `:in-body?`; `definition-occurrences` is\n   626\tthe store-key query carrying each binding row's path and\n   627\t`:conditional?`; `application-sites` is the application-row query.\n   628\tLoading is `yin.vm.ast-walker/vm-load-rows`.\n   629\t\n   630\t### 5.2 `:yin.semantic/code` (the semantic VM)\n   631\t\n   632\t```clojure\n   633\t{:format              :yin.semantic/code\n   634\t :contract            \"v2\"\n   635\t :identity-fn         jing/segment-key\n   636\t :identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?\n   637\t :row-defect-fn       yin.vm.code/well-formed-vector?\n   638\t :validate-fn         yin.vm.code/well-formed-vector?\n   639\t :obligations-fn      semantic-free-names\n   640\t :definitions-fn      semantic-definitions\n   641\t :applications-fn     semantic-application-sites\n   642\t :parts-fn            (constantly nil)}\n   643\t```\n   644\t\n   645\tPayload: the canonical positional instruction tuple vector (UCF section\n   646\t7.3.2), stored as the exact vector at its own `segment-key`; nothing\n   647\telse may hash there (UCF section 7.3.4). The identity is that address.\n   648\t`well-formed-vector?` is the section 7.5 grammar. `semantic-free-names`\n   649\tscans `:var` operands not bound by an enclosing closure's params, the\n   650\t`$code` query of section 7.7; `semantic-application-sites` scans the\n   651\tcall opcodes, including calls of imported names and of primitives\n   652\tthat receive a function argument; all three return the section 4.1\n   653\trecords. The linker module defines them, as B6 defined the two de\n   654\tBruijn scanners. The contract stamp is UCF's\n   655\t`{:yin.code/contract \"v2\"}`; a link request for this format carries the\n   656\tstamp, and the receiver's index is keyed per stamp (UCF section 7.3.3).\n   657\tLoading is `yin.vm.semantic/load-vector`, which writes the address to the\n   658\timage and the alias column.\n   659\t\n   660\t### 5.3 `:yin.debruijn.code` (the stack VM)\n   661\t\n   662\t```clojure\n   663\t{:format              :yin.debruijn.code\n   664\t :contract            \"b1\"\n   665\t :identity-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-hash\n   666\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [H v] (= H (yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-hash v)))\n   667\t :row-defect-fn       yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-defect\n   668\t :validate-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-defect\n   669\t :obligations-fn      stack-free-names\n   670\t :definitions-fn      stack-definitions\n   671\t :applications-fn     stack-application-sites\n   672\t :parts-fn            (constantly nil)}\n   673\t```\n   674\t\n   675\tUnchanged from B6 section 5.1 in substance. The identity H is\n   676\t`image-hash` over the descriptor hash (which embeds the lowering contract\n   677\tversion) and the canonical vector; the `=` here compares two values of\n   678\tone contract-pinned hash and is not a Class 3 site. Free names are\n   679\t`:load-free` operands; application sites are `:call` operands,\n   680\tincluding calls of imported names and function-argument primitives.\n   681\tLoading is `yin.vm.debruijn.stack/load-image`;\n   682\t`yin.repl`'s `append-stack-image` shows the relocation a second image\n   683\tneeds beside a held one.\n   684\t\n   685\t### 5.4 `:yin.debruijn.register` (the register VM)\n   686\t\n   687\t```clojure\n   688\t{:format              :yin.debruijn.register\n   689\t :contract            \"r1\"\n   690\t :identity-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-hash\n   691\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [R v]\n  1520\taddress. It replaces the `{sym fn}` dictionary entry.\n  1521\t\n  1522\t```clojure\n  1523\t{:yin.module/name        'my.lib\n  1524\t :yin.module/schema      1                   ; this container's shape\n  1525\t :yin.module/contracts   {:yin.ast/code          \"v2\"   ; per format\n  1526\t                          :yin.semantic/code     \"v2\"\n  1527\t                          :yin.debruijn.code     \"b1\"\n  1528\t                          :yin.debruijn.register \"r1\"}\n  1529\t :yin.module/tree        :segment/...        ; the one canonical tree\n  1530\t :yin.module/derivations {:yin.semantic/code     :segment/...  ; record\n  1531\t                          :yin.debruijn.code     :segment/...  ; record\n  1532\t                          :yin.debruijn.register :segment/...} ; record\n  1533\t :yin.module/index       {H :segment/... R :segment/...}       ; optional\n  1534\t :yin.module/exports     #{'foo 'bar}\n  1535\t :yin.module/requires    {'other.lib :segment/...}             ; manifest\n  1536\t :yin.module/primitives  {'println :yin.k.pp/sha256-...}       ; profile\n  1537\t :yin.module/footprint   {:store-keys #{} :effects #{}}}       ; UCF 7.6.1\n  1538\t```\n  1539\t\n  1540\tRules:\n  1541\t\n  1542\t- **One tree.** `:yin.module/tree` is the root row id of the canonical\n  1543\t  AST the module was authored as. The `:yin.ast/code` image *is* this\n  1544\t  tree, so it has no derivation record.\n  1545\t- **One derivation record per lowered format.** Each value under\n  1546\t  `:yin.module/derivations` is the address of a content-addressed\n  1547\t  derivation record in the shape `yin.vm.ledger/derive-record` mints:\n  1548\t  `{:yin.ledger/op :derive :yin.ledger/input tree\n  1549\t  :yin.ledger/output identity :yin.ledger/function f\n  1550\t  :yin.ledger/profile {...}}`. The linker fetches the record (through a\n  1551\t  `:yin.ledger/record` format record: `segment-matches?` identity, a\n  1552\t  validator over these keys, no parts, no obligations) and checks\n  1553\t  `:yin.ledger/input` equals `:yin.module/tree` and `:yin.ledger/output`\n  1554\t  is the identity it then fetches. A record leading from a different\n  1555\t  tree, or to a different identity, is `:derivation-mismatch`. Four\n  1556\t  individually valid images from four different trees therefore cannot\n  1557\t  share a manifest, and a swapped image fails before load.\n  1558\t- **Three contracts, kept apart.** A manifest carries a schema version\n  1559\t  and a per-format contract map, and neither is the other:\n  1560\t  - `:yin.module/schema` versions the manifest container itself: which\n  1561\t    keys exist and what they mean. It is checked by the\n  1562\t    `:yin.module/manifest` format record's validator, which implements\n  1563\t    exactly one schema version; a manifest of another version is\n  1564\t    `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:schema`. It says nothing about any\n  1565\t    bytecode.\n  1566\t  - `:yin.module/contracts` maps each format the manifest lowered to\n  1858\t`dao.agent.md`, `dao.agent.harness.md`, `dao.agent.mcp.server.md`) and\n  1859\tthe orchestrator log. Mark `yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md` as superseded by\n  1860\tthis document in its status line. No behavior changes. The B6 test\n  1861\tsuite passes unchanged apart from the require alias.\n  1862\t\n  1863\t**M2. Four format records.** Replace `:hash-fn` with `:identity-fn` and\n  1864\t`:identity-matches-fn`; rename `:free-names-fn` to `:obligations-fn`;\n  1865\tadd `:contract`, `:row-defect-fn`, and `:parts-fn`; add `ast-format`,\n  1866\t`semantic-format`, `semantic-free-names`, and `row-local-defect`. Make\n  1867\tstep 2 the bounded worklist. `yin.vm.content` keeps `materialize-tree!`\n  1868\tand `materialize-vector!` as the mint side (they are `publish!` for those\n  1869\tformats); `load-rows` and `fetch-vector` are retired, and their callers\n  1870\tmove to `fetch` with the new records. Tests, beyond B6's matrix for the\n  1871\ttwo new formats: a tree with one absent child row is `:absent` naming\n  1872\tthat row; a tree with one corrupt child row is `:address-mismatch`\n  1873\tnaming it; a tree whose root is well-formed but whose child has a bad\n  1874\ttag is `:descriptor-defect` with no fetch of that child's slots; a tree\n  1875\texceeding `:max-parts` is `:parts-limit`; a vector whose index entry\n  1876\tpoints at a different valid vector is `:hash-mismatch`; a vector minted\n  1877\tunder `:sha256` verifies against its own address while the default is\n  1878\t`:blake3`.\n  1879\t\n  1880\t**M3. Stepped core and link runtime.** Implement `link-state`,\n  1881\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon` over `dao.jing.remote.step` (or, for a\n   685\t   (section 5.3).\"\n   686\t  {:format              :yin.debruijn.code,\n   687\t   :contract            \"b1\",\n   688\t   :identity-fn         debruijn-code/image-hash,\n   689\t   :identity-matches-fn (fn [H v] (= H (debruijn-code/image-hash v))),\n   690\t   :row-defect-fn       debruijn-code/image-defect,\n   691\t   :validate-fn         debruijn-code/image-defect,\n   692\t   :obligations-fn      stack-free-occurrences,\n   693\t   :definitions-fn      vector-definition-occurrences,\n   694\t   :applications-fn     vector-application-sites,\n   695\t   :parts-fn            (constantly nil)})\n   696\t\n   697\t\n   698\t(def register-format\n   699\t  \"The `:yin.debruijn.register` format record: register images identified\n   700\t   by R under the \\\"r1\\\" contract, one image map per image. Free names\n   701\t   are `[:load-free rd name]` operands across all bodies, definitions\n   702\t   the `:store-put` keys, application sites the call opcodes\n   703\t   (section 5.4).\"\n   704\t  {:format              :yin.debruijn.register,\n   705\t   :contract            \"r1\",\n   706\t   :identity-fn         debruijn-register-code/register-hash,\n   707\t   :identity-matches-fn (fn [R v]\n   708\t                          (= R (debruijn-register-code/register-hash v))),\n   709\t   :row-defect-fn       debruijn-register-code/register-image-defect,\n   710\t   :validate-fn         debruijn-register-code/register-image-defect,\n   711\t   :obligations-fn      register-free-occurrences,\n   712\t   :definitions-fn      register-definition-occurrences,\n   713\t   :applications-fn     register-application-sites,\n   714\t   :parts-fn            (constantly nil)})\n   715\t\n   716\t\n   717\t(def semantic-format\n   718\t  \"The `:yin.semantic/code` format record: the canonical positional\n   719\t   instruction vector stored as the exact payload at its own\n   720\t   `segment-key` (UCF section 7.3.4), under the \\\"v2\\\" contract. Identity\n   721\t   and address are one preimage; step 3 still runs, because it is the\n   722\t   only check that the index did not point the identity at a different,\n   723\t   correctly stored payload (section 4.2). Free names are `:var`\n   724\t   operands, definitions `:store-put` operands, application sites the\n   725\t   call opcodes (section 5.2).\"\n   726\t  {:format              :yin.semantic/code,\n   727\t   :contract            \"v2\",\n   728\t   :identity-fn         jing/segment-key,\n   729\t   :identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?,\n   730\t   :row-defect-fn       code/well-formed-vector?,\n   731\t   :validate-fn         code/well-formed-vector?,\n   732\t   :obligations-fn      semantic-free-occurrences,\n   733\t   :definitions-fn      vector-definition-occurrences,\n   734\t   :applications-fn     vector-application-sites,\n   735\t   :parts-fn            (constantly nil)})\n   736\t\n   737\t\n   738\t(def ast-format\n   739\t  \"The `:yin.ast/code` format record: one row body `[tag & slots]` per\n   740\t   address (D3), the root row's id the tree's identity, under the \\\"v2\\\"\n   741\t   contract. Step 2 is a bounded worklist over the grammar's\n   742\t   `node`/`nodes` slots; the whole tree is assembled for step 4 by\n   743\t   prepending each part's address, the shape `validate-rows` takes. All\n   744\t   three scanners are Datalog over the rows, position-bearing by\n   745\t   occurrence path (section 5.1).\"\n   746\t  {:format              :yin.ast/code,\n   747\t   :contract            \"v2\",\n   748\t   :identity-fn         jing/segment-key,\n   749\t   :identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?,\n   750\t   :row-defect-fn       row-local-defect,\n   751\t   :validate-fn         vm/validate-rows,\n   752\t   :obligations-fn      tree-free-name-occurrences,\n   753\t   :definitions-fn      tree-definition-occurrences,\n   754\t   :applications-fn     tree-application-sites,\n   755\t   :parts-fn            body-child-ids})\n   756\t\n   757\t\n   758\t;; =============================================================================\n   759\t;; The H and R indexes (section 6)\n   760\t;; =============================================================================\n   761\t\n   762\t(defn address-attribute\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
