shadow (nth row 2))))\n   980\t      (get (:store st) (nth row 2)))))\n   981\t\n   982\t\n   983\t(defn- record-event\n   984\t  [st event-row*]\n   985\t  (update st :events conj event-row*))\n   986\t\n   987\t\n414:(defn- admit\n431:              catalogue-error (fn [h & kvs] {:error (apply malformed :harvest-catalogue :ordinal h kvs)})\n438:                    (cond (not= i h) (reduced (catalogue-error h))\n439:                          (nil? d) (reduced (catalogue-error h :tree j :path path))\n441:                          (reduced (catalogue-error h :tree j :path path))\n460:                                  (catalogue-error nil :tree j :path p)))\n896:(defn- harvest\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The core idea is promising—making definitions syntax would remove the shadowable callee—but several proof obligations remain in the proposal. In particular, the current VM accepts composition-supplied effectful functions, and the expander can start with an existing macro store. I’m separating consequences for definition soundness from broader claims about store-write discovery."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md | sed -n '1362,1392p;2010,2025p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | sed -n '91,112p;118,151p;1380,1435p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '559,594p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linearize.cljc | sed -n '104,160p'\nnl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md | sed -n '186,206p;756,777p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md | sed -n '1362,1392p;2010,2025p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | sed -n '91,112p;118,151p;1380,1435p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc | sed -n '559,594p'\nnl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linearize.cljc | sed -n '104,160p'\nnl -ba docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md | sed -n '186,206p;756,777p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1362\tbinding, which left a missing parameter name absent from the extended\n  1363\tenvironment rather than explicitly `nil` — so it could fall through to\n  1364\twhatever the closure's own captured environment (or, transitively, the\n  1365\tstore/primitives/modules chain) had under that name. Implemented as a\n  1366\tsingle shared helper, `yin.vm.engine/bind-params`, called from every\n  1367\tclosure-application site in both v2 evaluators\n  1368\t(`yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:192,513,555`, `yin/vm/semantic.cljc:200`);\n  1369\tthe v1 ast-walker this rule originally also described no longer exists,\n  1370\tdeleted by `yin.vm.v1-retirement.implementation-plan.md`. A missing\n  1371\tparameter is `nil` and shadows any such fallthrough within the closure's\n  1372\tbody. This is independent of §4.5's free/bound decision: it is about\n  1373\tparameter binding at closure application, not about resolving a name to\n  1374\ta value.\n  1375\t\n  1376\tEvery retained obligation is a required primitive or module export, checked by\n  1377\tprofile (UCF §7.5.2), and the **effects of a callable are read from its\n  1378\tprofile** (`:yin.k/effects`), never inferred from the name: `yin/def`\n  1379\tcontributes `:vm/store-put` and `require` contributes `:module/require`\n  1380\tbecause their profiles say so. Where a retained name has no profile at the\n  1381\temitter, discovery is `:incomplete`; conservatively retaining every\n  1382\tpossible primitive and module requirement is always admissible and never\n  1383\tmakes a `:complete` result wrong.\n  1384\t\n  1385\tThis rule is the amendment UCF §7.6.1's *Names* paragraph needs: its\n  1386\tsentence that a name \"is satisfied if it is bound in any environment the\n  1387\tvalue carries\" is the unsound test, and this document states the\n  1388\tcorrect rule in its place; UCF must be amended to say the same\n  1389\t(§10.8).\n  1390\t\n  1391\t#### 7.7.3 The fixed point converges over work items, not addresses\n  1392\t\n  2010\t   equal. What\n  2011\t   remains is the transitional hand printer's disclosed residuals\n  2012\t   (scalar metadata, pathological symbols, byte-array identity hashing,\n  2013\t   ambient print-var bindings on scalars — `dao.jing.md`'s Open Items)\n  2014\t   and the eventual pinned byte encoding itself, neither of which this\n  2015\t   design closes.\n  2016\t2. **The store-key domain is the `data` domain** (§2.2): every validator,\n  2017\t   extraction query, and store-slice encoding must use that one\n  2018\t   definition. This document now states it uniformly; the implementation\n  2019\t   phase must not reintroduce a narrower one, and the corpus must contain\n  2020\t   a numeric key beside the keyword one.\n  2021\t3. **Complete occurrence identity** (§2.5, §5.3, §8.4). Source origins\n  2022\t   `[:source medium batch j]` are supplied to lowering by the D4 envelope\n  2023\t   and recorded in instruction provenance: `medium` is the program stream's\n  2024\t   logical identity, `batch` is the composition-minted token, and `j` is the\n  2025\t   member index. Initial and\n    91\t    \"Returns the current continuation (what to do next).\n    92\t     VM-specific: linked frames, stack vector, call-stack, etc.\"))\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\t;; Primitive operations\n    96\t;; Arithmetic and comparison ops are direct clojure.core references.\n    97\t;; Wrapped only where VM semantics require it:\n    98\t;; - rest: clojure.core/rest returns a lazy seq; wrapped to return a vector\n    99\t;;   so that conj appends rather than prepends.\n   100\t;; - /: only the JVM throws on an integral zero divisor; JS and Dart divide\n   101\t;;   IEEE-754 and yield Infinity, so checked-divide makes the error\n   102\t;;   host-uniform.\n   103\t;; - yin/def, require: return effect descriptors consumed by the engine.\n   104\t(defn- checked-divide\n   105\t  \"clojure.core `/` except a zero divisor throws on every host.\n   106\t\n   107\t   JVM `/` throws `Divide by zero` for integral division only; JS and Dart\n   108\t   yield Infinity, so `(/ 1 0)` through the VM silently evaluated to `##Inf`\n   109\t   on those hosts. The REPL corpus pins divide-by-zero as an error with this\n   110\t   text on both evaluators (docs/design/yin.vm.divergence-register.md).\n   111\t   JS and Dart cannot distinguish `0` from `0.0`, so no rule reproduces the\n   112\t   JVM's double-division `##Inf` cross-host; the uniform error is the\n   118\t   (/ x y))\n   119\t  ([x y & more] (reduce checked-divide (checked-divide x y) more)))\n   120\t\n   121\t\n   122\t(defn primitive-profile\n   123\t  \"Build UCF §7.5.2's published profile record for `name`.\n   124\t\n   125\t   The address covers the name and all four semantic declarations. The name\n   126\t   remains the registry key rather than being duplicated in the returned\n   127\t   record. Profile values contain no host function objects and are therefore\n   128\t   ordinary portable data.\"\n   129\t  [name class arities effects host-state]\n   130\t  (let [description {:yin.k/name name,\n   131\t                     :yin.k/class class,\n   132\t                     :yin.k/arities (vec arities),\n   133\t                     :yin.k/effects (set effects),\n   134\t                     :yin.k/host-state host-state}\n   135\t        digest (jing/content-hash description {:algorithm :sha256})]\n   136\t    {:yin.k/profile (keyword \"yin.k.pp\" (str \"sha256-\" digest)),\n   137\t     :yin.k/class class,\n   138\t     :yin.k/arities (vec arities),\n   139\t     :yin.k/effects (set effects),\n   140\t     :yin.k/host-state host-state}))\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t(defn primitive-function\n   144\t  \"Return the executable value published by a primitive registry entry.\n   145\t\n   146\t   Bare entries remain supported for composition-supplied legacy registries.\"\n   147\t  [entry]\n   148\t  (if (and (map? entry) (contains? entry :yin.k/function))\n   149\t    (:yin.k/function entry)\n   150\t    entry))\n   151\t\n  1380\t;; supply the fixed point's inputs; the value, name-satisfaction, and\n  1381\t;; module parts remain the walk UCF §7.6.1 specifies. Free names are\n  1382\t;; `free-names` above; everything else the syntactic queries fill is here.\n  1383\t\n  1384\t(def footprint-table\n  1385\t  \"§7.7.1's effect normalization as a data value, keyed by the execution\n  1386\t   contract stamp (UCF §7.3.3) — the effect a syntax tag or mnemonic raises\n  1387\t   is part of that contract, lifted out of the reference machine's hot loop\n  1388\t   (`semantic.cljc`). Two directions: `:tags` over every §2.3 syntax tag\n  1389\t   and `:mnemonics` over every §2.4 mnemonic, each to the set of effect\n  1390\t   identifiers it contributes. Every tag and every mnemonic has a row, so\n  1391\t   \\\"no external effect\\\" is an explicit `#{}`, never an absence; a tag or\n  1392\t   mnemonic outside the table is `:yin.k/undecodable`, the outcome the\n  1393\t   validators give it — and the extraction queries' tag/mnemonic sets are\n  1394\t   table subsets, so over validated rows the lookup is total. The design\n  1395\t   table's tag↔mnemonic correspondence is 1:1 for the effect rows and\n  1396\t   deliberately lumped for the last (5 tags lower to 9 mnemonics; see\n  1397\t   `yin.vm.linearize`), so it is not re-stated as a map here. Its \\\"other\n  1398\t   requirement\\\" column is realized by the extraction queries themselves:\n  1399\t   an FFI op goes to the receiver-capability requirement\n  1400\t   (`:yin.k/ffi-ops` — the pair's own store keys are never a store-slice\n  1401\t   requirement, UCF §7.6.2), a store key to the store slice, a parked id\n  1402\t   to the parked-record obligation, and a call's effects are its callee's\n  1403\t   profile effects (§7.7.2). A `:variable`'s name obligation is\n  1404\t   conditional on freeness (§4.5) — a query (`free-names`), not a\n  1405\t   per-tag footprint fact.\"\n  1406\t  {\"v2\"\n  1407\t   {:tags {:stream/make #{:stream/make},\n  1408\t           :stream/put #{:stream/put},\n  1409\t           :stream/cursor #{:stream/cursor},\n  1410\t           :stream/next #{:stream/next},\n  1411\t           :stream/close #{:stream/close},\n  1412\t           ;; an FFI call is not an effect kind: it goes through the FFI pair\n  1413\t           :dao.stream.apply/call #{},\n  1414\t           :vm/park #{},                        ; scheduler-internal\n  1415\t           :vm/resume #{},\n  1416\t           :vm/gensym #{},                      ; the id counter is machine state\n  1417\t           :vm/store-get #{},\n  1418\t           :vm/store-put #{},\n  1419\t           :vm/current-continuation #{},\n  1420\t           ;; from syntax alone; a call's effects are its callee's profile\n  1421\t           :literal #{}, :variable #{}, :lambda #{}, :application #{}, :if #{}},\n  1422\t    :mnemonics {:stream-make #{:stream/make},\n  1423\t                :stream-put #{:stream/put},\n  1424\t                :stream-cursor #{:stream/cursor},\n  1425\t                :stream-next #{:stream/next},\n  1426\t                :stream-close #{:stream/close},\n  1427\t                :ffi-call #{},\n  1428\t                :park #{},\n  1429\t                :resume #{},\n  1430\t                :gensym #{},\n  1431\t                :store-get #{},\n  1432\t                :store-put #{},\n  1433\t                :current-continuation #{},\n  1434\t                :const #{}, :var #{}, :closure #{}, :push #{}, :call #{},\n  1435\t                :return #{}, :jump #{}, :branch-false #{}, :halt #{}}}})\n   559\t          pc-of (zipmap instructions (range))\n   560\t          resolve-ref (fn [e ref]\n   561\t                        (or (get pc-of ref)\n   562\t                            (throw (ex-info\n   563\t                                     \"Ref resolves to no instruction of this segment\"\n   564\t                                     {:entity e, :ref ref}))))\n   565\t          decode (fn [e]\n   566\t                   (let [ia (get attrs e)\n   567\t                         mnem (:yin.code/op ia)\n   568\t                         opcode (or (get vm/opcode-table\n   569\t                                         (get mnemonic-aliases mnem mnem))\n   570\t                                    (throw (ex-info \"Mnemonic has no opcode\"\n   571\t                                                    {:op mnem, :entity e})))]\n   572\t                     (case mnem\n   573\t                       :const [opcode (:yin.code/value ia)]\n   574\t                       :var [opcode (:yin.code/name ia)]\n   575\t                       :closure [opcode (:yin.code/params ia)\n   576\t                                 (resolve-ref e (:yin.code/body ia))]\n   577\t                       :call (if (:yin.code/tail? ia)\n   578\t                               [(:tailcall vm/opcode-table) (:yin.code/argc ia)]\n   579\t                               [opcode (:yin.code/argc ia)])\n   580\t                       :return [opcode]\n   581\t                       :jump [opcode (resolve-ref e (:yin.code/target ia))]\n   582\t                       :branch-false [opcode\n   583\t                                      (resolve-ref e (:yin.code/target ia))]\n   584\t                       :halt [opcode]\n   585\t                       :gensym [opcode (or (:yin.code/prefix ia) \"id\")]\n   586\t                       :store-get [opcode (:yin.code/key ia)]\n   587\t                       :store-put [opcode (:yin.code/key ia)\n   588\t                                   (:yin.code/value ia)]\n   589\t                       :stream-make [opcode (or (:yin.code/buffer ia)\n   590\t                                                vm/default-stream-capacity)]\n   591\t                       :stream-put [opcode]\n   592\t                       :stream-cursor [opcode]\n   593\t                       :stream-next [opcode]\n   594\t                       :stream-close [opcode]\n   104\t         [e]\n   105\t         (let [type (get-attr e :yin/type)]\n   106\t           (case type\n   107\t             :literal (emit! e [:const (get-attr e :yin/value)])\n   108\t             :variable (let [free (get-attr e :yin.resolved/free)]\n   109\t                         (emit! e (if (some? free)\n   110\t                                    [:load-free free]\n   111\t                                    [:load-bound (get-attr e :yin.resolved/depth)\n   112\t                                     (get-attr e :yin.resolved/position)])))\n   113\t             :lambda (let [l (fresh!)]\n   114\t                       (swap! bodies conj [l e (get-attr e :yin/body)])\n   115\t                       (emit! e [:closure (get-attr e :yin.resolved/arity) l]))\n   116\t             :application (let [operands (get-attr e :yin/operands)]\n   117\t                            (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/operator))\n   118\t                            (emit! e [:push])\n   119\t                            (doseq [o operands]\n   120\t                              (lower-node o)\n   121\t                              (emit! e [:push]))\n   122\t                            (emit! e [:call (count operands)\n   123\t                                      (boolean (get-attr e :yin/tail?))]))\n   124\t             :if (let [else (fresh!), end (fresh!)]\n   125\t                   (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/test))\n   126\t                   (emit! e [:branch-false else])\n   127\t                   (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/consequent))\n   128\t                   (emit! e [:jump end])\n   129\t                   (mark! else)\n   130\t                   (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/alternate))\n   131\t                   (mark! end))\n   132\t             :dao.stream.apply/call (let [operands (get-attr e :yin/operands)]\n   133\t                                      (doseq [o operands]\n   134\t                                        (lower-node o)\n   135\t                                        (emit! e [:push]))\n   136\t                                      (emit! e [:ffi-call (get-attr e :yin/op)\n   137\t                                                (count operands)]))\n   138\t             :stream/make (emit! e [:stream-make (get-attr e :yin/buffer)])\n   139\t             :stream/put (do (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/target))\n   140\t                             (emit! e [:push])\n   141\t                             (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/val-node))\n   142\t                             (emit! e [:stream-put]))\n   143\t             :stream/cursor (do (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/source))\n   144\t                                (emit! e [:stream-cursor]))\n   145\t             :stream/next (do (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/source))\n   146\t                              (emit! e [:stream-next]))\n   147\t             :stream/close (do (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/source))\n   148\t                               (emit! e [:stream-close]))\n   149\t             :vm/gensym (emit! e [:gensym (get-attr e :yin/prefix)])\n   150\t             :vm/store-get (emit! e [:store-get (get-attr e :yin/key)])\n   151\t             :vm/store-put (emit! e [:store-put (get-attr e :yin/key)\n   152\t                                     (get-attr e :yin/value)])\n   153\t             :vm/park (emit! e [:park])\n   154\t             :vm/current-continuation (emit! e [:current-continuation])\n   155\t             :vm/resume (do (lower-node (get-attr e :yin/val-node))\n   156\t                            (emit! e [:resume (get-attr e :yin/parked-id)]))\n   157\t             (throw (ex-info (str \"Cannot lower-stack resolved node of type \" type)\n   158\t                             {:type type, :entity e})))))]\n   159\t      (lower-node root)\n   160\t      (emit! root [:halt])\n   186\t### 2.2 Definition shape\n   187\t\n   188\tA harvested path must resolve to an `:application` equivalent to:\n   189\t\n   190\t```clojure\n   191\t(yin/def <literal-symbol> value)\n   192\t```\n   193\t\n   194\tIt has an operator `[:variable yin/def]`, exactly two operands, a first operand\n   195\t`[:literal sym]` where `sym` is a symbol, and a value subtree rooted at the\n   196\tsecond operand. A declared occurrence additionally requires a `:lambda` value\n   197\troot. No `:macro?` slot exists.\n   198\t\n   199\tEvery definition path must be harvested, including definitions in unexecuted\n   200\tbranches and non-running trees. Every harvest entry must resolve to this shape.\n   201\tMissing, duplicate, out-of-range, or non-definition entries fail with\n   202\t`:harvest-catalogue`; a declaration outside the catalogue or on a non-lambda\n   203\tdefinition fails with `:stray-macro-declaration`.\n   204\t\n   205\t### 2.3 Call site\n   206\t\n   756\texpanded tree packet, and event rows. `(reset)` rebuilds expander and evaluator\n   757\tstate. `repl-state` lists macro names and lambda root addresses.\n   758\t\n   759\t### 10.2 Frontends and encoder\n   760\t\n   761\tFrontends identify macro-defining source forms. The encoder projects every\n   762\ttree to rows, emits one packet per root or disconnected definition tree, emits\n   763\tone harvest row per definition in source declaration order, and emits one\n   764\tdeclaration row per macro definition.\n   765\t\n   766\t`yang.clojure` lowers `defmacro` to ordinary `yin/def` syntax and supplies the\n   767\tdeclaration occurrence; it puts no macro metadata in the lambda row.\n   768\t`yang.python` and `yang.php` require no lookup: every call is an ordinary\n   769\tapplication row. A future macro-definition surface in either language need\n   770\tonly produce the same declaration and harvest rows.\n   771\t\n   772\t### 10.3 Builds and cross-platform behavior\n   773\t\n   774\tA build composes the same observer between file-backed media. Addresses remain\n   775\tstable across storage, streams, expansion, and evaluation. Persistent\n   776\tprovenance stores log packets unchanged or indexes event rows as a separate\n   777\tinterpretation. Store seeding folds any validated sequence of input batches in\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
