on outside the catalogue or on a non-lambda\n   203\tdefinition fails with `:stray-macro-declaration`.\n   204\t\n   205\t### 2.3 Call site\n   206\t\n   207\tA call site is an occurrence of `:application` whose operator occurrence is a\n   208\t`:variable` naming a stored macro and is not shadowed by an enclosing lambda's\n   209\tparameters. Operands are canonical syntax trees. Frontends do no macro lookup,\n   210\tdiscovery, or argument coercion. A macro name in operand position is an\n   211\tordinary variable; a lambda in operator position is an ordinary lambda.\n   212\t\n   213\t### 2.4 Output\n   240\tvalid-tree?  : tree-packet opts → nil | error-data\n   241\tmark-tail    : tree-packet → tree-packet\n   242\tstep         : expander → expander\n   243\tdrain-errors : expander → [expander' summary]\n   244\t```\n   245\t\n   246\t```clojure\n   247\t{:store       {sym macro-tree}\n   248\t :incarnation {:yin.expander/token uuid}\n   249\t :attempt     0\n   250\t :source-medium opaque-medium-token\n   251\t :t           0\n   252\t :guards      {:max-depth 100\n   370\tenclosing lambda parameter slots, and `path` is the occurrence path.\n   371\t\n   372\t```text\n   373\tmacro-of(ctx, operator-address, shadow):\n   374\t  row = index[operator-address]\n   375\t  when row.tag == :variable and row.name not in shadow:\n   376\t    return ctx.store[row.name]\n   377\t  otherwise return nil\n   378\t```\n   379\t\n   380\tThere is no inline macro-lambda case. Transformer authority comes only from a\n   381\tvalidated declaration harvested into the store.\n   382\t\n   383\t### 4.2 `expand-node`\n   384\t\n   385\t```text\n   386\texpand-node(state, address, path, shadow, depth, origin):\n   387\t  row = state.index[address]\n   388\t\n   389\t  if row.tag == :application and macro-of(ctx, row.operator, shadow):\n   390\t    attempt = allocate-attempt(ctx)\n   391\t    event   = begin-event(attempt, origin, state.root, path, macro-root)\n   392\t    if depth >= max-depth:\n   393\t      fail(event, {:kind :depth-guard, :depth depth, :path path})\n   394\t    operands = [subtree-packet(index, child) for child in row.operands]\n   395\t    output   = invoke(macro-tree, operands, ctx)\n   396\t    validate output, allowing working stand-ins but no batch metadata\n  1822\t  (all of its occurrences carry the declaration or none do, which is\n  1823\t  automatic for a legacy entity with one flag). The declaration catalogue\n  1824\t  is derived from the validated harvest catalogue and the declarations,\n  1825\t  never carried separately, so it cannot disagree with either. A\n  1826\t  violation is an admission failure `{:kind :malformed-input :reason\n  1827\t  :harvest-catalogue}` naming the entry.\n  1828\t- **Binding.** A declaration `[j path :yin.macro/definition]` names the\n  1829\t  `:application` at `path` in tree `j`, and through the catalogue the\n  1830\t  original definition whose group contains `[j path]`; that node must be\n  1831\t  `(yin/def <literal sym> <lambda>)`, i.e., its reconstructed semantic map must have an `:operator` that is a `:variable` node naming `yin/def` (free at that site, per §4.5), its first operand a `:literal` symbol node, and its second operand a `:lambda` node. A\n  1832\t  declaration whose coordinates do not resolve to such a node is an\n  1833\t  admission failure, `{:kind :malformed-input :reason\n  1834\t  :stray-macro-declaration}`, the successor of §3.1 step 1's\n  1835\t  `:stray-macro-lambda`.\n  1836\t- **Marks are validated before they are stripped.** A frontend or the\n  1837\t  §9.1 adapter that converts a map AST carrying `:macro? true` must reject\n  1838\t  a flagged lambda anywhere but the value operand of a `yin/def` as\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
