node; `id` is `(jing/segment-key [tag & slots])`.\n   794\t\n   795\t(def semantic-bytecode-grammar\n   796\t  \"The §2.3 tag table: tag -> ordered `[field kind]` slots. Position `i` of a\n   797\t   row body (after the tag) holds the map field named at `i`, so this one\n   798\t   table drives both projection and reconstruction.\"\n   799\t  {:literal [[:value :data]],\n   800\t   :variable [[:name :sym]],\n   801\t   :lambda [[:params :syms] [:body :node]],\n   802\t   :application [[:operator :node] [:operands :nodes] [:tail? :bool]],\n   803\t   :if [[:test :node] [:consequent :node] [:alternate :node]],\n   804\t   :dao.stream.apply/call [[:op :kw] [:operands :nodes]],\n   805\t   :vm/gensym [[:prefix :str]],\n   806\t   :vm/store-get [[:key :key]],\n   807\t   :vm/store-put [[:key :key] [:val :data]],\n   808\t   :vm/current-continuation [],\n   809\t   :vm/park [],\n   810\t   :vm/resume [[:parked-id :kw] [:val :node]],\n   811\t   :stream/make [[:buffer :int]],\n   812\t   :stream/put [[:target :node] [:val :node]],\n  1380\t;; supply the fixed point's inputs; the value, name-satisfaction, and\n  1381\t;; module parts remain the walk UCF §7.6.1 specifies. Free names are\n  1382\t;; `free-names` above; everything else the syntactic queries fill is here.\n  1383\t\n  1384\t(def footprint-table\n  1385\t  \"§7.7.1's effect normalization as a data value, keyed by the execution\n  1386\t   contract stamp (UCF §7.3.3) — the effect a syntax tag or mnemonic raises\n  1387\t   is part of that contract, lifted out of the reference machine's hot loop\n  1388\t   (`semantic.cljc`). Two directions: `:tags` over every §2.3 syntax tag\n  1389\t   and `:mnemonics` over every §2.4 mnemonic, each to the set of effect\n  1390\t   identifiers it contributes. Every tag and every mnemonic has a row, so\n  1391\t   \\\"no external effect\\\" is an explicit `#{}`, never an absence; a tag or\n  1392\t   mnemonic outside the table is `:yin.k/undecodable`, the outcome the\n  1393\t   validators give it — and the extraction queries' tag/mnemonic sets are\n  1394\t   table subsets, so over validated rows the lookup is total. The design\n  1395\t   table's tag↔mnemonic correspondence is 1:1 for the effect rows and\n  1396\t   deliberately lumped for the last (5 tags lower to 9 mnemonics; see\n  1397\t   `yin.vm.linearize`), so it is not re-stated as a map here. Its \\\"other\n  1398\t   requirement\\\" column is realized by the extraction queries themselves:\n  1399\t   an FFI op goes to the receiver-capability requirement\n  1400\t   (`:yin.k/ffi-ops` — the pair's own store keys are never a store-slice\n   705\t  [^ASTWalkerVM vm]\n   706\t  (engine/vm-value vm))\n   707\t\n   708\t\n   709\t(defn vm-load-program\n   710\t  \"Load one datom batch into the VM: the existing datom-to-AST conversion\n   711\t   plus the execution-field updates. This is the loader host composition\n   712\t   hands to `dao.stream.observer/run-on-stream` alongside\n   713\t   `engine/ready-for-ingress?` and the VM's runner.\"\n   714\t  [^ASTWalkerVM vm datoms]\n   715\t  (let [ast (vm/datoms->ast datoms)]\n   716\t    (assoc vm\n   717\t           :program ast\n   718\t           :control ast\n   719\t           :halted? false\n   720\t           :blocked? false\n   721\t           :value nil)))\n   722\t\n   723\t\n   724\t(defn vm-load-rows\n   845\t                                   :control nil,\n   846\t                                   :env env,\n   847\t                                   :k nil,\n   848\t                                   :value nil,\n   849\t                                   :halted? true,\n   850\t                                   :blocked? false}))\n   851\t         (telemetry/install :ast-walker)\n   852\t         (ffi/attach (:bridge opts))\n   853\t         (telemetry/emit-snapshot :init)))))\n   640\t;; Row-local validation and the parts worklist (sections 5.1, 4.2 step 2)\n   641\t;; =============================================================================\n   642\t\n   643\t(defn row-local-defect\n   644\t  \"The section 7.4 row-local rules -- `:tag`, `:arity`, `:slot-kind`,\n   645\t   `:saturation` -- over one row body `[tag & slots]`, nil when the body\n   646\t   is locally well formed. The whole-tree rules (`:id-resolves`,\n   647\t   `:acyclic`, `:root-reachable`) cannot run over one body and are never\n   648\t   reported here: a locally well-formed body's child ids resolve in\n   649\t   step 2's worklist. A malformed row's slots are never followed\n   650\t   (section 5.1). A body that is not a vector is a `:tag` defect: only a\n   651\t   vector can be a row.\"\n   652\t  [body]\n   653\t  (let [row (if (vector? body) (into [::root] body) [::root body])\n   654\t        res (vm/validate-rows {:root ::root, :rows {::root row}})]\n   655\t    (when (contains? #{:tag :arity :slot-kind :saturation} (:rule res))\n   656\t      res)))\n   657\t\n   658\t\n   659\t(defn- body-child-ids\n   660\t  \"The child row ids of one fetched body's `node`/`nodes` slots, by the\n   661\t   grammar's own positions. Only valid segment addresses are followed: a\n   662\t   slot holding something else stays in the row for `validate-rows` to\n   663\t   name as its `:slot-kind` defect, exactly as it would in a\n   664\t   hand-supplied row set.\"\n   665\t  [body]\n   666\t  (let [slots (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (first body))]\n   667\t    (when (and slots (= (count slots) (dec (count body))))\n   668\t      (mapcat (fn [[_field kind] v]\n   669\t                (case kind\n   670\t                  :node (when (jing/segment-address? v) [v])\n   671\t                  :nodes (filter jing/segment-address? v)\n   672\t                  nil))\n   673\t              slots (rest body)))))\n   674\t\n   675\t\n   676\t;; =============================================================================\n   677\t;; Format records (section 5)\n   678\t;; =============================================================================\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
