  450\t   receiver-side half refuses an operator the receiver's own env or\n   451\t   store already binds, as `:shadowed-free`). Proving the primitive\n   452\t   binding against a verified module manifest is an M4 refinement; the\n   453\t   footprint is the whole static proof here, and over-retaining\n   454\t   obligations is always admissible (section 4.1).\"\n   455\t  [tree]\n   456\t  (let [{:keys [root db occ]} (tree-rows tree)\n   457\t        defs (->> (query/collect\n   458\t                    (query/q tree-definition-query db occ root))\n   459\t                  (map (fn [[key path]]\n   460\t                         (let [row (tree-row-at tree path)\n   461\t                               yin-def? (and row\n   462\t                                             (= :application\n   463\t                                                (nth row 1)))\n   464\t                               at-path (if yin-def?\n   465\t                                         (conj path [3 2])\n   466\t                                         path)\n   467\t                               [_ conditional?]\n   468\t                               (tree-enclosure tree at-path)]\n   469\t                           {:name key, :at [root at-path],\n   470\t                            :yin-def? yin-def?,\n   785\t;; `yin.vm.engine/resolve-var` uses: free env -> store -> primitives ->\n   786\t;; module registry. A name the image publisher meant as a primitive or a\n   787\t;; module binding must resolve there; a receiver whose free env or store\n   788\t;; also binds it would bind it differently, so that is refused as\n   789\t;; shadowed rather than executed (D11).\n   790\t\n   791\t(defn- obligation-name\n   792\t  \"The name an obligation carries: a section 4.1 record's `:name`, or\n   793\t   the bare name itself.\"\n   794\t  [obligation]\n   795\t  (if (map? obligation) (:name obligation) obligation))\n   796\t\n   797\t\n   798\t(defn- shadowed?\n   799\t  [{:keys [free-env store]} obligation]\n   800\t  (let [sym (obligation-name obligation)]\n   801\t    (or (contains? free-env sym) (contains? store sym))))\n   802\t\n   803\t\n   804\t(defn- resolvable?\n   805\t  [{:keys [primitives modules]} obligation]\n   806\t  (let [sym (obligation-name obligation)]\n   807\t    (or (contains? primitives sym)\n   808\t        (some (fn [k] (and (map? k) (= sym (:name k))))\n   809\t              (keys primitives))\n   810\t        (and (symbol? sym)\n   811\t             (some? (namespace sym))\n   812\t             (some? (module/resolve-module\n   813\t                      modules\n   814\t                      (symbol (str (namespace sym) \".\" (name sym)))))))))\n   815\t\n    55\t   Mirrors `yin.vm.linearize/flatten-program`'s own case dispatch, read\n    56\t   from the same `:yin/*` attributes, but as data instead of code.\"\n    57\t  {:application [[:yin/operator :child] [:yin/operands :children]]\n    58\t   :dao.stream.apply/call [[:yin/operands :children]]\n    59\t   :if [[:yin/test :child] [:yin/consequent :child] [:yin/alternate :child]]\n    60\t   :stream/put [[:yin/target :child] [:yin/val-node :child]]\n    61\t   :stream/cursor [[:yin/source :child]]\n    62\t   :stream/next [[:yin/source :child]]\n    63\t   :stream/close [[:yin/source :child]]\n    64\t   :vm/resume [[:yin/val-node :child]]})\n    65\t\n    66\t\n    67\t(def ^:private unsupported-types\n    68\t  \"Node types outside both evaluators' supported corpus, matching\n    69\t   `yin.vm.linearize/unsupported` exactly -- read here, not required\n    70\t   from there, since that namespace stays untouched.\"\n    71\t  #{:yin/macro-expand :vm/store-update})\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t;; =============================================================================\n    75\t;; resolve: named datoms -> resolved tuples + provenance side table\n    76\t;; =============================================================================\n    77\t\n    78\t(defn- reject-host-value!\n   475\tsemantic VM has no opcode for it, and no test constructs one (a search of\n   476\t`test/` for the node type on 2026-09-14 found none). Its one reachable\n   477\tpath is an in-process, hand-built map AST handed straight to the walker;\n   478\tno row can carry it (§2.2, `data`), so it never crosses the boundary in\n   479\teither direction.\n   480\t\n   481\tThe orchestrator's alternative, a `:fn` slot restricted to a named\n   482\tprimitive symbol resolved and profile-checked per UCF §7.5.2, is not\n   483\tadopted: it would re-admit a node that no persistent form carries, for a\n   484\tconvenience no corpus program uses.\n   485\t\n   486\tA program that needs the behaviour writes it as an application of the\n   487\t`yin/def` primitive (`v2.cljc:128`) over a `:vm/store-get` operand:\n   488\t`(yin/def k (f (vm/store-get k) args…))`. That rewrite is equivalent to\n   489\tthe arm **only under stated conditions**, and this document does not claim\n   490\tit as a general semantics-preserving migration:\n   491\t\n   492\t- `yin/def` and `f` resolve through `resolve-var`'s precedence, store\n   493\t  → primitives → modules (`src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:46-58`), so the\n   494\t  rewrite is equivalent only when neither `yin/def` nor `f` is shadowed by an enclosing `:lambda`'s params at the site (so both resolve as free names, through the fallthrough, rather than to a local binding);\n   495\t- the arm stores whatever `(apply f current args)` returns, as data\n   496\t  (`ast_walker.cljc:410-415`), while an application interprets an\n   497\t  effect-shaped return (`ast_walker.cljc:184-188`,\n   498\t  `semantic.cljc:206-220`). An effect descriptor is itself plain data:\n   499\t  `module/effect?` recognizes any map carrying `:effect`\n   500\t  (`src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:77-79`), and\n   501\t  `{:effect :vm/store-put :key :x :val 4}` passes `plain-data?`. So the\n   502\t  rewrite is equivalent only when `f` returns plain data **that is not an\n   503\t  effect descriptor under the applicable execution contract**; a result\n   504\t  the contract would interpret is stored by the arm and executed by the\n   505\t  rewrite.\n  1368\t(`yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:192,513,555`, `yin/vm/semantic.cljc:200`);\n  1369\tthe v1 ast-walker this rule originally also described no longer exists,\n  1370\tdeleted by `yin.vm.v1-retirement.implementation-plan.md`. A missing\n  1371\tparameter is `nil` and shadows any such fallthrough within the closure's\n  1372\tbody. This is independent of §4.5's free/bound decision: it is about\n  1373\tparameter binding at closure application, not about resolving a name to\n  1374\ta value.\n  1375\t\n  1376\tEvery retained obligation is a required primitive or module export, checked by\n  1377\tprofile (UCF §7.5.2), and the **effects of a callable are read from its\n  1378\tprofile** (`:yin.k/effects`), never inferred from the name: `yin/def`\n  1379\tcontributes `:vm/store-put` and `require` contributes `:module/require`\n  1380\tbecause their profiles say so. Where a retained name has no profile at the\n  1381\temitter, discovery is `:incomplete`; conservatively retaining every\n  1382\tpossible primitive and module requirement is always admissible and never\n  1383\tmakes a `:complete` result wrong.\n  1384\t\n  1385\tThis rule is the amendment UCF §7.6.1's *Names* paragraph needs: its\n  1386\tsentence that a name \"is satisfied if it is bound in any environment the\n  1387\tvalue carries\" is the unsound test, and this document states the\n  1388\tcorrect rule in its place; UCF must be amended to say the same\n  1389\t(§10.8).\n  1390\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
